          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Marked extensional well-founded orders are important in constructing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cumulative+hierarchy"} cumulative hierarchy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in a model of set theory, in the same way that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-orders"} well-orders
            or sets with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+relation"} transitive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+relation"} extensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-founded+relations"} well-founded relations
            are important in constructing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinals"} ordinals
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            where one cannot in general show that the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinals"} cardinals
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and the set of ordinals in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            are in bijection with each other.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong marked extensional well-founded order
            or
            %strong mewo
            is a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+relation"} extensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-founded+relation"} well-founded relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \prec b
            on a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(a)
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#marked_elements Marked elements
          %p
            An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
            is
            %strong marked
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x)
            is true. By the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+schema+of+bounded+separation"} axiom schema of bounded separation
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi S
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_S \coloneqq \{x \in S \vert m(x)\}
          %h3#marked_extensional_wellfounded_order_homomorphisms Marked extensional well-founded order homomorphisms
          %p
            A
            %strong marked extensional well-founded order homomorphism
            between two marked extensional well-founded order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S \to T
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                preserves the marking predicate: for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x)
                implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(f(x))
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                preserves the well-founded relation: for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in S
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≺
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \prec y
                implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≺
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \prec f(y)
          %p
            A
            %strong marked extensional well-founded order isomorphism
            is a marked extensional well-founded order homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S \to T
            with a marked extensional well-founded order homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:T \to S
            such that for all elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(f(s)) = s
            and for all elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(g(t)) = t
          %p
            The category of marked extensional well-founded order homomorphisms is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} MEWO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{MEWO}
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are marked extensional well-founded orders and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are marked extensional well-founded order homomorphisms.
          %h3#trivialization Trivialization
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} MEWO
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} EWO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U:\mathrm{MEWO} \to \mathrm{EWO}
            which takes a marked extensional well-founded order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≺
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \prec, m)
            to its underlying extensional well-founded order
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≺
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \prec)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} EWO
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} MEWO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:\mathrm{EWO} \to \mathrm{MEWO}
            which takes an extensional well-founded order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ≺
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \prec)
            to the marked extensional well-founded order
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≺
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊤
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S, \prec, \top_S)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊤
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top_S
            is the always true predicate on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %strong trivialization
            of a marked extensional well-founded order is defined as the composite of the two functors above
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{S} \coloneqq F(U(S))
          %h3#simulations Simulations
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simulation"} simulation
            between marked extensional well-founded orders
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a marked extensional well-founded order homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S \to T
            such that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            is downwards closed: for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ≺
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \prec f(x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in S
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \prec x
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≺
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(z) \prec y
          %p
            We denote the set of simulations between marked extensional well-founded orders
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊑
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sqsubseteq T
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} MEWO
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sim
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{MEWO}_\mathrm{Sim}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} MEWO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{MEWO}
            whose objects are marked extensional well-founded orders and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are simulations. We show that the above category is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %p
            Since the relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≺
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prec
            is extensional and well-founded, the following is true of simulations:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every simulation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S \to T
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            %li
              %p
                Given marked extensional well-founded orders
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊑
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sqsubseteq T
                has at most one element.
          %p
            As a result, one could define the relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \leq T
            on marked extensional well-founded orders by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi x
                    %mo .
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊑
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists x.x \in S \sqsubseteq T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \leq T
            between marked extensional well-founded orders is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
          %ul
            %li
              for all marked extensional well-founded orders
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \leq S
            %li
              for all marked extensional well-founded orders
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi T
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \leq T \wedge T \leq U \implies S \leq U
            %li
              for all marked extensional well-founded orders
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi T
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \leq T \wedge T \leq S \implies S = T
          %h3#covered_elements_and_initial_segments Covered elements and initial segments
          %p
            An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
            is
            %strong covered
            if there exists a marked element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in S
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \prec y
            is true. Given a marked extensional well-founded order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and an element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
            %strong initial segment
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the set of all elements covered by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mo +
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi t
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \downarrow^+ x \coloneqq \{t \in S \vert t \prec x\}
          %p
            The initial segment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mo +
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \downarrow^+ x
            is a marked extensional well-founded order, with the well-founded relation defined as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \prec z
            for elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mo +
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in S \downarrow^+ x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo +
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in S \downarrow^+ x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x(y) \coloneqq y \prec x
            for elements
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo +
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in S \downarrow^+ x
          %p
            A marked extensional well-founded order is
            %strong covered
            if every element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
            is covered; i.e.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo .
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mo .
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≺
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x \in S.\exists y \in S.m(y) \wedge (x \prec y)
          %p
            It follows by well-founded induction that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %mo +
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \downarrow^+ x
            is a covered marked extensional well-founded order.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given a marked extensional well-founded order
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi S
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S \downarrow^+ x \to \overline{S}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:S \downarrow^+ x \to S
              and the canonical function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi S
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j:S \to \overline{S}
              given by the identity function on the carrier set, is a simulation.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given a marked extensional well-founded order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo +
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi S
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo +
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \downarrow^+ x = S \downarrow^+ y
              implies that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = y
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given marked extensional well-founded orders
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              and a function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S \to T
              which preserves the marking predicate; i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(x)
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(f(x))
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a simulation if and only if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi T
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mo +
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \downarrow^+ x = T \downarrow^+ f(x)
          %h3#bounded_simulations Bounded simulations
          %p
            A bounded simulation between marked extensional well-founded orders
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            consists of a marked element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in M_T
            and a simulation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:S \to T
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is equal to the initial segment at
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi T
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mo +
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{im}(f) = T \downarrow^+ y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊏
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sqsubset T
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given marked extensional well-founded orders
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊏
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \sqsubset T
              has at most one element.
          %p
            As a result, one could define the relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \lt T
            on marked extensional well-founded orders by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi x
                    %mo .
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊏
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists x.x \in S \sqsubset T
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for all marked extensional well-founded orders
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \lt T
                implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ≤
                      %mover
                        %mi T
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \leq \overline{T}
            %li
              %p
                for all marked extensional well-founded orders
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \lt T
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \lt U
                implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ≤
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \leq \overline{U}
            %li
              %p
                for all marked extensional well-founded orders
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \lt T
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \leq U
                implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \lt U
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-order"} well-order
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+relation"} extensional relation
